 ("ul", ["**Regular polygons:** a triangle has 3 sides, a square 4, a pentagon 5, a hexagon 6, … each has one more side than the one before.", "**Matchstick patterns:** squares in a row use 4, 7, 10, 13, … sticks (add 3 each time). Triangles in a row use 3, 5, 7, 9, … sticks (add 2 each time), which is 2 × n + 1.", "**Complete graph:** join every pair of n points. 2 points need 1 line, 3 points need 3, 4 points need 6, 5 points need 10, 6 points need 15, 7 points need 21. These are triangular numbers. For 7 points: 6 + 5 + 4 + 3 + 2 + 1 = 21. The same count gives the handshakes among n friends and the matches in a league of n teams (n points, each pair once).", "**Koch snowflake:** start with an equilateral triangle. On each segment, replace the middle one-third by two sides of a smaller triangle. The number of segments goes 3, 12, 48, 192, … (×4 each time) while each new segment is one-third as long, so the border keeps getting longer."]),
 ("note", "NOTE", "The Koch snowflake is a **fractal**: if you zoom in on any edge you see the same bumpy shape again and again. It shows how a very simple rule, repeated many times, can create a very complicated picture."),
